00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:52.460
The Trumpeter at the Start Line

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:52.460
Now they know about our plans

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:54.520
to charge on through, huh?

00:02:57.230 --> 00:02:58.070
But jeez,

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:02.510
Dame Adele, that's one heavy armored mechanic shell!

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:05.310
Oh, this? My father left it to me.

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:08.580
It's my first time using it in battle,
so sorry if something goes wrong.

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:11.870
No worries.

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:17.320
<i>If only Naomasa and Mitotsudaira were here...</i>

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:30.520
Okay, guys...

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:34.750
I, Student Council Clerk Toussaint Neshinbara,

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:38.480
am going to be the strategist for this battle.

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:41.760
Naito, how's the situation over there?

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:43.070
<i>Yup, yup!</i>

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:44.770
<i>Gacchan, you're up.</i>

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:49.730
Kitano Tenmangu Shrine
Special Port for Musashi

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.500
<i>For starters, here's Musashi.</i>

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:51.530
<i>All of this is a mountainous corridor,</i>

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:55.900
Kitano Tenmangu Shrine

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:53.400
<i>and here's a checkpoint.</i>

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:56.560
<i>Here's the western meeting grounds.</i>

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:56.900
Kitano Tenmangu Shrine
Western Meeting Grounds

00:03:56.560 --> 00:04:00.550
<i>That's where they positioned their
fortress-style cluster formation, Tercio.</i>

00:03:56.900 --> 00:04:00.530
Kitano Tenmangu Shrine

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:03.840
There are three guard ships protecting the skies.

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:06.750
The interrogation warship is at this land port.

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:09.100
Land Port for Normal Ships

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:08.770
That's where Horizon is.

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:12.460
So, that's essentially our goal.

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:14.650
Hey, Mr. Fanfic Writer.

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:20.130
Are those salty Tercio guys in
my foolish brother's way?

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:21.400
Indeed.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:23.430
Tercio is a major battle formation.

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:27.480
This cluster formation has musketeers
encompass the oblong pikemen battalion.

00:04:28.010 --> 00:04:31.440
With musketeers at each corner,
it resembles a fortress.

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:34.440
It's slow moving, but excels at defense.

00:04:34.930 --> 00:04:36.530
Defense, huh?

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:39.090
The enemy doesn't need to win.

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:44.580
All they have to do is keep us at bay
until Ariadust commits suicide.

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:47.890
They will do two things to see that happens.

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:50.220
They'll seal off the roads for one.

00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:52.730
Then, they will seal off the sky.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:56.710
Kitano Tenmangu Shrine

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:02.710
Kitano Tenmangu Shrine
STANDBY

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:03.800
Kitano Tenmangu Shrine
DIVINE TRANSMISSION

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:08.370
Hey, guys, could you hear me out?

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:11.490
<i>I don't think anyone likes war.</i>

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:15.910
<i>But if you agree that there is value
in living life to the fullest,</i>

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.810
Emergency Exit

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:18.730
<i>then I think that battlefields where
you'll die if you don't persevere</i>

00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:21.060
<i>are places overflowing with value.</i>

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:26.670
<i>I don't know if everyone is fighting
of their own volition or not,</i>

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:29.090
<i>but let's think positively if you're gonna fight!</i>

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:34.310
<i>So guys, do you have friends who
would rescue you from danger?</i>

00:05:34.750 --> 00:05:37.690
<i>Do you have a name to call out to when all is lost?</i>

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:43.050
<i>Although somewhat silly, do you have
the noble belief that you're a hero?</i>

00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:44.520
<i>And most importantly,</i>

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:48.300
<i>do you have a place to go back to,
characters in a story?</i>

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:54.290
Now, let me explain the plot.

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:54.710
Asama Shrine
Special Port for Musashi

00:05:54.710 --> 00:05:57.270
Asama Shrine

00:05:55.610 --> 00:05:58.820
The path we must take is straight through.

00:05:59.270 --> 00:06:02.480
The giants K.P.A. Italia and Tres España

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:05.720
have stationed cluster formations, heroes,

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:07.550
aerial battleships and Gods of War.

00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:12.040
If we defeat them, retrieve Horizon Ariadust

00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:14.260
and obtain her Armor of Deadly Sins,

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:19.590
nations will be forced to take note
of Musashi's military might.

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:26.670
So, will you go and fight, characters?

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:30.200
Charge straight through
and bring our story to a climax!

00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:34.200
So, Protagonist, why don't you
make a statement already?

00:06:35.470 --> 00:06:37.660
Hey, where'd our protagonist go?

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:51.010
<i>Hey!</i>

00:06:51.380 --> 00:06:52.220
What?!

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:55.120
You're so slow! What's keeping you?

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:56.720
They're waiting for us!

00:06:56.720 --> 00:06:59.270
Wh..Why are you running ahead?

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:01.960
Why ask? Aren't we going over there?

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:05.320
D..Don't do it!

00:07:06.130 --> 00:07:07.700
F..Follow him!

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:08.990
Yeah!

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:11.780
Whoohoo!

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:16.260
I made it!

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:18.540
Open sesame!

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:28.040
Fire!

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:32.650
Whoa, whoa! They're firing already?

00:07:33.500 --> 00:07:35.140
This sucks!

00:07:35.650 --> 00:07:37.000
Protect our chancellor!

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:39.370
Yeah!

00:07:46.790 --> 00:07:48.320
Now, now...

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:52.200
What now?
Hey, what's with that?

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:03.460
I finally caught up...

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:06.670
Um, uh...

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:08.500
Bull's eye!

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:13.120
Owie...

00:08:13.540 --> 00:08:15.390
What the heck was that about?

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:17.010
D..Dame Adele?!

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:18.580
You okay?

00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:20.130
A heavy armored retainer?

00:08:20.130 --> 00:08:22.030
Just how old is that thing?

00:08:22.550 --> 00:08:25.310
Wow, that's amazing!

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:28.410
Normally, you'd be in big trouble
if you took a direct hit.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:35.240
I remember a retainer in my old land
had a rather old mechanic shell...

00:08:35.590 --> 00:08:39.870
<i>Neshinbara, do you know why Adele's
become so friggin' invincible?</i>

00:08:40.390 --> 00:08:44.570
Armor for knights and retainers
is mass-produced nowadays,

00:08:44.570 --> 00:08:47.420
but they used to be customized and made to order.

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:49.840
The times have probably come full circle.

00:08:50.180 --> 00:08:52.460
<i>What do you mean by that?</i>

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:55.580
Before the battlefield focused on speed,

00:08:55.580 --> 00:08:57.370
they designed super-heavy armor

00:08:57.370 --> 00:09:00.250
that could handle getting shot at.

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:02.430
I think Balfetto's is one of those.

00:09:02.670 --> 00:09:08.440
<i>It's so slow it's obsolete in our speed-focused battles.</i>

00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:10.570
<i>But it's a good wall.</i>

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:12.440
<i>How dare you call it a "wall"?!</i>

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:14.820
<i>I can't believe you guys!</i>

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.340
Balfetto, calm down.

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:18.820
<i>A heavy armor reduced to being a mere wall?</i>

00:09:23.400 --> 00:09:25.250
Has something pleased you?

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:28.390
No, I'm hardly pleased.

00:09:28.390 --> 00:09:31.670
After all, Musashi's representatives are out fighting.

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:39.760
Ow, ow, ow!

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:41.720
I made it...

00:09:42.610 --> 00:09:43.560
Huh?!

00:09:45.650 --> 00:09:48.150
Why is everyone standing behind me?

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:50.150
Don't let it bug you, Adele!

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:52.760
We're supporting your continued existence!

00:09:52.760 --> 00:09:55.610
You make it sound so deep!

00:09:56.630 --> 00:09:58.360
What's happening?

00:09:58.570 --> 00:09:59.820
Okey-dokey!

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:03.450
P-Boy will cover for your lack of mobility,
so it's all good, Adele!

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:06.000
That's not where your value resides right now anyway.

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:10.550
No!

00:10:10.550 --> 00:10:14.840
Please don't shoot!

00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:17.260
Youch!

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:22.350
Our escape route!

00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:24.680
They'll fire if you try to retreat.

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:28.350
BARRIER

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:30.890
Now they're firing at us?

00:10:31.140 --> 00:10:34.200
They're trying to keep us from sending anything out.

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:36.280
AUTO             AUTO             AUTO

00:10:45.390 --> 00:10:46.140
BARRIER

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:48.730
BARRIER

00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:50.980
BARRIER

00:10:56.050 --> 00:10:57.220
<i>Lady Musashi!</i>

00:10:57.220 --> 00:10:59.310
<i>I have detected changes in the high ether</i>

00:10:59.310 --> 00:11:01.470
<i>output in Tres España's guard ship.</i>

00:11:01.830 --> 00:11:03.700
<i>It's coming from their primary Ether Cannon.</i>

00:11:03.700 --> 00:11:05.240
<i>They have commenced a spell.</i>

00:11:05.240 --> 00:11:05.720
<i>Over.</i>

00:11:09.210 --> 00:11:10.890
BARRIER

00:11:21.420 --> 00:11:22.790
<i>Well done!</i>

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:23.490
<i>Over.</i>

00:11:23.970 --> 00:11:26.560
They weren't taking us seriously with that shot.

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:27.450
The next one...

00:11:27.740 --> 00:11:28.910
...will be a direct hit.

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:32.480
<i>They're firing their second shot!</i>

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:33.170
<i>Over.</i>

00:11:35.260 --> 00:11:38.260
<i>Lady Asama, I am counting on you. Over.</i>

00:11:39.230 --> 00:11:43.720
The Asama Shrine will use its
power to protect Musashi.

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:53.300
The respective area has been purified!

00:11:57.960 --> 00:12:01.070
Connect to White Sand Plinth "Ume-Tsubaki."

00:12:13.430 --> 00:12:17.000
Determine usage of Energy 2
in roughly five hundred meters.

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:18.210
Clap!

00:12:18.940 --> 00:12:21.110
Energy

00:12:21.150 --> 00:12:23.610
Asama Shrine

00:12:23.610 --> 00:12:24.570
Asama Shrine
MEET UP

00:12:23.740 --> 00:12:24.590
Got it.

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:52.000
<i>I have detected the sound of a God of War launching.</i>

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:53.540
<i>Over.</i>

00:12:53.990 --> 00:12:57.050
You're up, Naito! Naruse!

00:13:03.630 --> 00:13:05.340
A God of War, huh?

00:13:05.610 --> 00:13:09.570
It would suck if they got around
our barrier and attacked Musashi.

00:13:09.570 --> 00:13:10.760
Right, Gacchan?

00:13:12.430 --> 00:13:16.710
But I never thought we'd get to fight
against Tsirhc as witches.

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:18.150
I know!

00:13:18.390 --> 00:13:22.760
The Tsirhc Church prioritized
condemning us out of fear,

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:24.680
which hampered our research.

00:13:24.680 --> 00:13:27.120
People had to practice these spells in hiding.

00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:28.030
It's techno-magic.

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:30.830
Musashi's made for a good sanctuary.

00:13:31.420 --> 00:13:32.450
In that case...

00:13:36.230 --> 00:13:40.040
Exposing ourselves as witches to
protect Musashi is worth it!

00:13:40.270 --> 00:13:42.170
Here he comes, Margot!

00:13:50.150 --> 00:13:51.640
["Verwandlung" is German for "metamorphosis."]

00:13:50.150 --> 00:13:51.640
Verwandlung!

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:18.420
Weiss Frauen!

00:14:21.280 --> 00:14:22.420
Schwarze Frauen!

00:14:23.080 --> 00:14:24.670
Come, Weiss Frauen!

00:14:25.140 --> 00:14:27.170
Come here, Schwarze Frauen!

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:29.360
Currently Preparing for Fusion
Please Exercise Caution

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:46.940
Zwei Frauen: Complete!

00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:24.460
That's a God of War for you.

00:15:24.460 --> 00:15:26.070
We didn't come close to destroying it!

00:15:26.380 --> 00:15:28.540
I want a good offensive spell.

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:30.360
Wanna increase Auspuff and up the pressure?

00:15:28.540 --> 00:15:30.360
["Auspuff" is German for "exhaust."]

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:31.950
He's too fast!

00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:46.670
Endure! I gotta endure!

00:15:47.050 --> 00:15:50.300
Sweet, she declared she can endure this,
so charge forward!

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:52.610
Eh?! N..Not again!

00:15:52.610 --> 00:15:54.510
This sucks!

00:16:00.510 --> 00:16:03.690
I hate ceremonious speech.

00:16:05.910 --> 00:16:07.630
A Tres España God of War

00:16:07.630 --> 00:16:11.310
has commenced battle with
Musashi's witches above Musashi.

00:16:13.730 --> 00:16:15.370
Witches, eh?

00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:22.710
It's questionable if we can deal with just
one God of War, wouldn't you say?

00:16:23.070 --> 00:16:26.820
It's no wonder they only had a couple
of these keep guard over Musashi.

00:16:35.740 --> 00:16:36.600
But!

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:37.850
We're...

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:41.310
...representing Musashi!

00:16:47.160 --> 00:16:48.960
He's in my sight.
Here's four shots!

00:17:00.930 --> 00:17:01.910
I'll get him!

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:22.180
Margot!

00:17:32.010 --> 00:17:35.890
Justice sides with those who obey the Testament!

00:17:35.890 --> 00:17:40.160
Justice sides with those who obey the Testament!

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:44.280
Justice sides with those who obey the Testament!

00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:00.600
Margot, get up!

00:18:00.940 --> 00:18:02.020
Margot!

00:18:03.820 --> 00:18:04.730
<i>Wake up!</i>

00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:08.190
We've entrusted Musashi's skies to you,

00:18:08.190 --> 00:18:10.390
so what'll happen if you don't protect them?!

00:18:10.390 --> 00:18:12.440
Show us the same grit as

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:14.910
when you stole my right as an Edel Brocken tester!

00:18:14.910 --> 00:18:19.460
Admiral, weren't you once ace of
Tres España's Gods of War?

00:18:19.460 --> 00:18:20.700
Please say something!

00:18:24.880 --> 00:18:26.910
Listen up, witches!

00:18:27.240 --> 00:18:32.570
Wasn't I the first one you defeated
out of everyone here?

00:18:32.930 --> 00:18:37.800
But I'm the strongest guy amongst us.

00:18:38.750 --> 00:18:42.350
<i>Got it? Then wake up, Zwei Frauen!</i>

00:18:51.340 --> 00:18:55.480
After that, unfold ten 200km/h acceleration spells.

00:18:56.020 --> 00:19:00.490
Make them fixed 1/10th sized models,
consuming 200 atell each.

00:19:00.920 --> 00:19:02.620
Gacchan's such a quick writer...

00:19:04.990 --> 00:19:06.950
he couldn't dodge every stroke.

00:19:08.320 --> 00:19:11.060
White magic creates plus power.

00:19:12.800 --> 00:19:15.710
Black magic creates minus power.

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:18.720
What do you think happens when
you combine the two?

00:19:20.110 --> 00:19:22.850
Ten rolls of ten yen coins worth 1,000 yen each.

00:19:23.330 --> 00:19:25.100
Let's go, average daily wages!

00:19:25.290 --> 00:19:26.470
Herrlich!

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:45.370
Schlag!

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:45.370
["Schlag" is German for "strike."]

00:19:54.820 --> 00:19:56.410
Sweet!

00:19:57.110 --> 00:19:58.760
They did it, Admiral!

00:20:09.740 --> 00:20:10.630
<i>You okay?</i>

00:20:11.030 --> 00:20:12.020
Neshinbara...

00:20:12.400 --> 00:20:14.410
We trashed a God of War.

00:20:14.410 --> 00:20:16.320
<i>Yeah, I saw.</i>

00:20:16.810 --> 00:20:18.440
<i>Thank you both so much.</i>

00:20:18.440 --> 00:20:19.500
<i>Come on back.</i>

00:20:19.500 --> 00:20:20.950
Judge.

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:25.790
Gacchan, you destroyed Weiss Frauen.

00:20:25.790 --> 00:20:26.990
Shush...

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:29.860
Gacchan, you're shaking?

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:31.610
So are you, Margot.

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:37.710
It's okay for now.

00:20:47.470 --> 00:20:49.470
The rest is up to you...

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:52.770
The God of War has been shot down.

00:20:52.970 --> 00:20:55.460
My, most impressive.

00:20:55.880 --> 00:20:58.880
So, how are our ground forces holding up?

00:20:58.880 --> 00:21:03.260
They are currently clashing with
Musashi's Chancellor and their army.

00:21:03.260 --> 00:21:04.480
They're "clashing"?

00:21:04.480 --> 00:21:06.200
This isn't a picnic, jeez!

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:11.200
The strong do not torment the weak
before annihilating them.

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:12.860
You crush them swiftly!

00:21:13.370 --> 00:21:16.920
The strong are supposed to show off
their immeasurable power.

00:21:17.180 --> 00:21:19.300
Crush them now.

00:21:34.010 --> 00:21:35.440
What the?!

00:21:38.100 --> 00:21:39.820
They split us up!

00:21:47.800 --> 00:21:49.150
Whoa!

00:21:49.150 --> 00:21:53.710
Everyone totally wants me right now!

00:21:53.710 --> 00:21:55.710
Shut up or you'll weaken our defenses!

00:21:55.710 --> 00:21:56.620
Back off!

00:21:56.850 --> 00:22:03.220
Help me please, officers!

00:22:04.490 --> 00:22:05.510
It's show time!

00:22:06.080 --> 00:22:07.570
I'm ready whenever.

00:22:07.570 --> 00:22:09.760
Indeed, I've grown tired of waiting.

00:22:14.640 --> 00:22:16.270
Let's go, Jizuri Suzaku!

00:22:24.760 --> 00:22:26.610
I have confirmed that they launched a God of War.

00:22:26.940 --> 00:22:28.320
It should be landing in the center

00:22:28.320 --> 00:22:30.320
of the western meeting grounds.

00:22:33.010 --> 00:22:34.790
Legend of the Ultimate Executors!

00:22:35.160 --> 00:22:38.930
Naito and Naruse secured the skies for us.

00:22:38.930 --> 00:22:40.250
Let's go wild, Mito!

00:22:40.420 --> 00:22:42.250
We are on our way...

00:22:43.550 --> 00:22:44.790
my king!

00:22:46.100 --> 00:22:50.260
Sora ni nozomu you ni

00:22:46.100 --> 00:22:50.260
Our voyage across the real world

00:22:50.540 --> 00:22:57.270
Koukai suru genjitsu sekai no tabi

00:22:50.540 --> 00:22:57.270
Is like navigating straight for the sky

00:22:57.770 --> 00:23:01.610
Nani mo mottenai kedo

00:22:57.770 --> 00:23:01.610
I may not have anything

00:23:02.120 --> 00:23:04.720
Kokoro no naka

00:23:02.120 --> 00:23:04.720
But I have a dream

00:23:04.720 --> 00:23:08.950
Kagayaita yume ga aru yo

00:23:04.720 --> 00:23:08.950
That's shone brightly in my heart

00:23:09.200 --> 00:23:11.790
Mada kikoenai

00:23:09.200 --> 00:23:11.790
I still haven't heard

00:23:11.790 --> 00:23:15.280
Kimi no hontou no mune no koe

00:23:11.790 --> 00:23:15.280
The voice spoken from your heart

00:23:15.580 --> 00:23:20.200
Shiritain da — sugao wo misete yo

00:23:15.580 --> 00:23:20.200
Let me in — show me the real you

00:23:20.200 --> 00:23:23.790
Barabara ni chirabatta

00:23:20.200 --> 00:23:23.790
We'll bury the void

00:23:23.790 --> 00:23:26.890
Ikutsu mo no piisu wo

00:23:23.790 --> 00:23:26.890
As we find all of the pieces

00:23:27.060 --> 00:23:29.560
Hitotsu zutsu sagashite

00:23:27.060 --> 00:23:29.560
That have gotten scattered around

00:23:29.560 --> 00:23:32.720
Kuuhaku wo umete iku no sa

00:23:29.560 --> 00:23:32.720
One piece at a time

00:23:32.720 --> 00:23:37.540
Ubawareta kimi no egao

00:23:32.720 --> 00:23:37.540
Your smile has been stolen

00:23:37.540 --> 00:23:41.210
Tori modosu tame ni hashiru yo

00:23:37.540 --> 00:23:41.210
But I will race to get it back

00:23:41.210 --> 00:23:47.150
Boku wa hikari sasu michi wo

00:23:41.210 --> 00:23:47.150
As I run down the shining path

00:24:07.150 --> 00:24:10.990
Next Episode
Musashi's Mr. Impossible
